Title: Welcome
Credit: a sample screenplay for Maugham
Author: You

INT. A SMALL APARTMENT - NIGHT

Rain on the window. A cold cup of tea. A WRITER sits in front of a blank page, and then she types.

What she types is a scene heading. In the binder on the left, it appears under the Script as a scene, with the page it starts on.

WRITER
(to herself)
Every scene heading is a scene. Click one in the binder and the script scrolls there.

She types a name in capitals, then a line under it. The page dresses itself: a character, then dialogue.

WRITER (CONT'D)
And when it guesses wrong, Tab cycles the line through what it could be. Shift-Tab goes back.

She presses ⌘2. Brief opens beside the script, and she writes one sentence about what this script is going for.

[[todo: Give the writer a name]]

EXT. THE SAME STREET - LATER

The rain has stopped. The WRITER walks, hands in her pockets, and the street lamps come on one after another.

WRITER
The to-do up there is waiting in To resolve. ⌘1, and there it is.

She stops under a lamp and looks back at the window she left.

WRITER (CONT'D)
The page count's in the line under the script, and a page target is set at its right end.

She presses ⌘/ for the sheet of everything Fountain can do, and reads it on the way home.

FADE OUT.
